Verse 1:
[Db]God's free mercy streameth [Gb/Db]over all the [Db]world,
[Bbm]And His [Ab/C]banner [Db]gleameth, [Gb]By His [Eb7/G]church [Bbm]unfuried;
[Ab7]Broad and deep [Bbm]and [Ab/C]glorious, [Db]As the heaven [Fm]above,
[Ab7/Gb]Shines in [Gb]might [Ab7/Gb]victorious [Gb]His eternal [Db]love.

Verse 2:
[Db]Summer suns are glowing [Gb/Db]over land and [Db]sea;
[Bbm]Happy [Ab/C]light [Cdim]is [Db]flowing, [Gb]Bountiful [Bbm]and [Ab7]free;
[Ab7]Everything [Ab/C]rejoices [Db]in the [Ebm]mellow [Gb]rays;
[Ab7/Gb]Earth's ten [Gb]thousand [Db/F]voices [Gb]swell the [Db/Ab]psalm [Ab7]of [Db]praise.

Verse 3:
[Db]Lord, upon our blindness [Gb/Db]thy pure radiance [Db]pour;
[Bbm]For Thy [Ab/C]loving [Db]kindness [Gb]we would [Eb7/G]love [Bbm]Thee [Ab7]more;
[Ab7]And when [Bbm]clouds [Ab/C]are [Db]drifting dark across [Fm]the [Gb]sky,
[Ab7/Gb]Then, the [Gb]veil [Ab7/Gb]uplifting, [Gb]father, [Db/Ab]be [Ab7]Thou [Db]nigh.

Verse 4:
[Db]We will never doubt Thee, [Gb/Db]tho' veil Thy light;
[Bbm]Life is [Ab/C]dark [Cdim]without [Db]Thee, [Gb]death with [Eb7/G]Thee [Bbm]is [Ab7]bright.
[Ab7]Light of [Bbm]light, [Ab/C]shine [Db]o'er us on our [Ebm]pilgrim [Gb]way,
[Ab7/Gb]Go Thou [Gb]still [Ab7/Gb]before [Bbm]us [Gb]to the [Db/Ab]endless day.
